    "result_text": "Full suite is green \u2014 **262 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement is that creating an owner must be rejected with HTTP 409 when the telephone number already belongs to any other owner. The codebase already had a duplicate-owner mechanism (`DuplicateOwnerException` \u2192 409 via the exception advice), but it keyed on last name + telephone. I changed it to key on telephone alone across all owners.\n\nChanges in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- `addOwner` now calls `isDuplicateTelephone(owner)` and throws with a telephone-specific message.\n- Replaced `isDuplicateOwner` (searched by last name, matched last name + telephone) with `isDuplicateTelephone`, which scans `findAllOwners()` and matches on telephone only.\n\nAlso updated the `DuplicateOwnerException` javadoc to describe the telephone rule, and added a test `createOwnerDuplicateTelephoneDifferentLastNameReturnsConflict` verifying that a matching telephone with a different last name returns 409. All existing owner tests (including \"same last name, different telephone succeeds\") still pass under the stricter rule.",
